# 11g's reply to it (#2466): the row (1, 'abc', 10), the LONG cell chunked
# (`fe 03 61 62 63 00`), then its ub2 indicator and ub2 return code, both 0,
# then the status.
# Captured 2026-11-06 through tools/capture_proxy.py: sqlplus 11.2 (instant
# client 11.2, x86-64 Linux, `set long 100000`) running `select id, l, n from
# pyo_drcp_lg order by id` on Oracle 11g XE 11.2.0.2 with SERVER=POOLED, the
# DRCP pool started, over rows (1, 'abc', 10), (2, NULL, 20) and
# (3, 30000 x's, 30). The TTC payload, without the packet's header, as
# `hexdump -C` output; the offset column and the |ascii| gutter are ignored by
# tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
